Tower shared floors: the split bar as an accordion (mockup, Nov 21). Stills and the clip on branch stills/tower-accordion; the code on this branch (no test link: it replaces the split bar).
Each boss's card is the lone bar itself (figure or portrait, name, LVL, meters, "58 moves left", his bar prop, his words), laid out once at the open width; each part is a window onto its card's LEFT side. Expanding only widens the window.
Widths: the open part 75% of the room the gaps and outlines leave, the folded ones the rest. Phone (390 wide): floor of 2, 266 open / 93 folded; floor of 3, 258 / 48 / 48. Computer (1280): floor of 3, 440 / 78 / 78.
Height unchanged: 95 px phone, 61 px computer; the board's size and place measured equal to main's (phone 334 px at y 149; computer 600 px at y 103 at 1x).
Timing: 300 ms ease (flex-grow) on a turn change and on a tap; reduced motion instant (checked: no transition runs). A tapped part stays open until the turn changes or it's tapped again; tapping the boss to move does nothing.
Stills: phone-floor-of-2.png, phone-floor-of-2-tapped-open.png, phone-floor-of-3.png, phone-floor-of-3-tapped-open.png, computer-floor-of-3.png, computer-floor-of-3-tapped-open.png. Clip: slide-turn-change.gif (Don Dough to Timber) and slide-turn-change-frames.png (every 50 ms).
Bosses: floor of 2 Jefferson + Hollow; phone floor of 3 Timber + Dash + Don Dough; computer Jefferson + Hollow + Don Dough. Babur's pump: in his card on a phone, beside his figure on a computer, as now.
Calls made: TO MOVE rides the top outline at the window's left (centered on a folded window); a phone's card has its name and status a size smaller and its prop room scaled to 82% (a lone bar is 362 x 99, the card 252-260 x 89).
For Eric 1: a folded boss who speaks (a passive's line on another boss's turn): his bubble is cut by his window (the white tail over Dash in the clip). Recommend: his bubble drawn over the bar beside his window, not inside it; or his part opens for the line.
For Eric 2: 75% on a phone's floor of 3 leaves 48 px folded (his figure about two-thirds shown) and a 252 px card (names to about 9 letters fit). 80% would give 266 / 33 / 33.
